-- CA_0240_record_2026_utah_primary_results.sql
--
-- Slot CA_0240 reserved via `npm run steward --prefix backend -- slot CA` (author: Chris Andrews).
-- No migration runner exists; this file records SQL applied by hand.
--
-- Stale-primaries batch 2: record the outcome of every 2026-06-23 UTAH primary row that still carried no
-- result — the Utah State House and Senate, the State Board of Education, and county offices in Salt
-- Lake, Utah and Davis counties. 153 rows reviewed: 152 written, 1 held. Same shape as CA_0231 /
-- CA_0237: set result, result_source, result_recorded_at.
--
--   won 128 · lost 16 · withdrew 5 · not_nominated 3 · held 1
--
-- HOW UTAH WORKS, AND WHY MOST ROWS ARE 'won' WITHOUT VOTES
--   Utah nominates by party convention and/or signatures, and prints a party primary ONLY when the race
--   is contested. 118 of our 139 Utah primary races hold a single candidate: that person is the nominee
--   without appearing on a primary ballot. For every row, the deciding document is the certified
--   GENERAL list — on it = the nominee ('won'); absent = not the nominee, with the reason taken from the
--   Lieutenant Governor's candidate-status list ("Out in Primary", "Out in Convention", "Withdrew"):
--     lost           16  lost a contested primary (votes in result_source)
--     not_nominated   3  "Out in Convention": Will Pierce (SBOE 14 R), Nicholas Roberts (SL County Sheriff
--                        R), Travis Hoban (Utah County Auditor R)
--     withdrew        5  Jeff Burton (HD64 R), MacKenzie Miller (SD11 D), Danielle Stratton (SBOE 14 D),
--                        Courtnee Justice (SBOE 14 R), J. Michael Clara (SBOE 5 R). Only the state's
--                        "Withdrew" status exists; no dated filing was found. 🔴 These five ALSO get
--                        candidate_status = 'withdrawn' — is_live_candidate() drops a row on status
--                        'withdrawn' or result 'not_nominated', and result 'withdrew' is neither
--                        (Phase 167 rule 6). No other row's candidate_status changes.
--
-- HELD (1): Rashelle Hobbs, "Salt Lake County Recorder". There is no Recorder race in 2026: she won the
--   seat on 2024-11-05 (Salt Lake County 2024 general certification, 250,018 / 233,025), so it is next up
--   in 2028. The 2026 primary race row is a seeding error, not a lost nomination; 'not_nominated' would
--   claim a contest that did not happen. Left NULL and reported.
--
-- SOURCES (fetched 2026-09-24)
--   State: the 2026 General Election Certification (signed by the Lieutenant Governor 2026-08-28; a
--     scanned PDF whose OCR mangles two names — Christofferson, Chevrier — checked against the text by
--     hand); the June 23 2026 Primary Election Statewide Canvass (votes for multi-county races); the
--     candidate filings status list (updated 2026-09-08).
--   Counties (single-county races, and county offices): Salt Lake County "FINAL OFFICIAL ELECTION
--     RESULTS" + Board of Canvassers letter 2026-07-07; Utah County "Official Results" + Board of
--     Canvassers certification 2026-07-07; Davis County "OFFICIAL RESULTS" 2026-07-07 + Certification of
--     Candidates 2026-08-31. The state results site still flags these counties isOfficialResults false;
--     the canvass documents are the official record, and its counts agree with them.
--   Close race: SBOE 11 R, Nuttall 10,297 / Hutchinson 10,020 (state canvass).
--   Fred J. Allen (Utah County Commission Seat B, D) is listed by the county as "J. ALLEN" — same race
--   and party; recorded as won with that noted in result_source.
--
-- OUT OF SCOPE: Utah's 12 U.S. House primary rows (Phase 167, Chris Cantrell). The November roster gap is
-- separate work: only 9 Utah legislative races exist on the 2026 general election, and the certified
-- general list names Forward, Constitution, Libertarian and unaffiliated candidates we do not have.
--
-- IDEMPOTENT: every write is guarded on result IS NULL (and status on its pre-image). Dry run: the body
-- wrapped BEGIN; ... ROLLBACK; against prod, applied twice in one transaction, then rolled back and
-- re-read. ROLLBACK (once applied): UPDATE essentials.race_candidates SET result = NULL,
--   result_source = NULL, result_recorded_at = NULL WHERE result_source LIKE '%Recorded by CA_0240
--   (2026-09-24).'; and restore candidate_status = 'active' on the five 'withdrew' rows.

BEGIN;

CREATE TEMP TABLE ca0240_result ON COMMIT DROP AS
SELECT v.rc_id, v.full_name, v.status_before, v.result, v.result_source
